IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wiv-dates`
IMPORT `wiv-rules`

-- Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic), formerly the Wage Theft Act 2020 -- the questions of a WORKER WHO
-- REPORTS UNDERPAYMENT (or other wrongdoing) to the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria, or is thinking of doing so. Each
-- question takes only plain facts (yes/no, dates, a choice from a list). The shared definitions, the repeal answers, the
-- s 71 regulative rule and the penalty table are in wiv-rules.l4.
--
-- Since 12 December 2025 the Act no longer makes wage theft an offence and no longer gives inspectors powers: those
-- questions are answered "it does not arise", naming the Wage Theft Amendment Act 2025.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Workforce
-- Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020, Version No. 005 (17 December 2025), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria;
-- published with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in
-- accordance with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 -- the worker who reports underpayment`

§§ `What became of the wage theft laws`

@export What does the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic), formerly the Wage Theft Act 2020, now say about one of its former provisions? The Wage Theft Amendment Act 2025 (No. 35/2025) repealed the wage theft offences (Part 2), the inspectors' powers (Part 4), Divisions 1 and 3 of Part 5 and some other sections from 12 December 2025. For anything on or after that day the provision does not arise; before 1 July 2021 the Act was not yet in operation; in between, the provision was in force but its text is not in this encoding.
GIVEN `which former provision` IS A `Former provision` @desc The former provision you are asking about (for example Part 2, the wage theft offences of dishonestly withholding employee entitlements and of falsifying or not keeping employee entitlement records; or Part 4, the inspectors and their powers)
      `the day it is about` IS A DATE @desc The day of the conduct or event you are asking about (for example the day your pay was withheld)
GIVETH A `What the Act says about it now`
`What does the Act now say about this former provision` MEANS
    `what the Act says now about a repealed provision on` `the day it is about`

@export Which section of the Wage Theft Amendment Act 2025 (Vic) (No. 35/2025) repealed this former provision of the Wage Theft Act 2020 (now the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020)? Each repeal commenced on 12 December 2025.
GIVEN `which former provision` IS A `Former provision` @desc The former provision you are asking about
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Which section of the Wage Theft Amendment Act 2025 repealed it` MEANS
    `the repealing section of the Wage Theft Amendment Act 2025 for` `which former provision`

@export Is it an offence under the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic), formerly the Wage Theft Act 2020, for my employer to dishonestly withhold my wages or other entitlements, or to falsify or fail to keep my pay records? The wage theft offences (Part 2, ss 6 to 18) were repealed by s 7 of the Wage Theft Amendment Act 2025 from 12 December 2025, so for conduct on or after that day the question does not arise under this Act. Other law (for example the Fair Work Act 2009 of the Commonwealth) may still apply; it is not encoded here.
GIVEN `the day it happened` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer withheld the money or dealt with the records
GIVETH A `What the Act says about it now`
`Is it an offence under this Act for my employer to withhold my wages` MEANS
    `what the Act says now about a repealed provision on` `the day it happened`

@export Can an inspector of the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria use powers under the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic) to enter my workplace or require my employer's records to look into my underpayment? The inspectors' powers (Part 4, ss 32 to 62) were repealed by s 20 of the Wage Theft Amendment Act 2025 from 12 December 2025, so on or after that day the question does not arise under this Act.
GIVEN `the day the power would be used` IS A DATE @desc The day the inspector would enter or require the records
GIVETH A `What the Act says about it now`
`Can an inspector use powers under this Act to look into my underpayment` MEANS
    `what the Act says now about a repealed provision on` `the day the power would be used`

§§ `Am I a worker, and what the Inspectorate does for me`

@export Am I a "worker" under the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic) s 3? A worker is a person who is or was employed (paid or as a volunteer), or engaged as an independent contractor, to work at or in relation to a workplace. A workplace includes residential premises where work is carried out, but not a part of premises that is someone's domestic home. Former workers count.
GIVEN `how am I or was I engaged` IS A `How I am or was engaged` @desc How you are, or were, engaged: employed on a paid basis; employed on a voluntary basis; engaged as an independent contractor; or none of these
      `where is the work` IS A `Where the work is` @desc Where the work is or was done: at or in relation to a workplace that is not residential premises (a shop, office, site, farm, vehicle and so on); at or in relation to residential premises where work is carried out, outside any part that is someone's domestic home; only in a part of premises that is someone's domestic home; or not at or in relation to any workplace
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I a worker` MEANS `s 3 -- worker` `how am I or was I engaged` `where is the work`

@export Is it a function of the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria to give me information, education and advice about my workplace entitlements (Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic) s 20(1)(ha))? Since 12 December 2025 it has the function of giving workers information, education and advice about "prescribed workplace entitlements matters", the matters the regulations prescribe (s 79(1)(a)). The regulations are not part of this encoding, so you are asked whether your matter is prescribed.
GIVEN `how am I or was I engaged` IS A `How I am or was engaged` @desc How you are, or were, engaged: employed on a paid basis; employed on a voluntary basis; engaged as an independent contractor; or none of these
      `where is the work` IS A `Where the work is` @desc Where the work is or was done (see the question "Am I a worker")
      `is my matter prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your matter (for example underpayment of wages) is a workplace entitlements matter prescribed by regulations under s 79(1)(a)
      `the day I ask` IS A DATE @desc The day you ask the Inspectorate
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Inspectorate advise me about my workplace entitlements` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the day I ask` `is before` `the day of the 2025 repeals and the name change` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (outside the sources: an earlier version, fork F3)
           IF (NOT (`s 3 -- worker` `how am I or was I engaged` `where is the work` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: "to workers")
           IF (NOT `is my matter prescribed`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: "prescribed")
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@export Can I complain to the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria about public construction, or give it information about public construction (Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic) s 20(1)(ia))? Since 17 December 2025 it has the function of receiving complaints or matters, and related information, regarding public construction from any person. Public construction is public construction within the meaning of the Project Development and Construction Management Act 1994, or construction prescribed by regulations.
GIVEN `is it public construction under the 1994 Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work is public construction within the meaning of the Project Development and Construction Management Act 1994 (broadly, construction by or for the State or a public body)
      `is it prescribed public construction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work is construction, or a class of construction, prescribed as public construction by regulations under s 79(1)(ab)
      `the day I complain` IS A DATE @desc The day you make the complaint or give the information
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I complain to the Inspectorate about public construction` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the day I complain` `is before` `the day of the public construction amendments and s 69A` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (outside the sources: an earlier version, fork F3)
           IF (NOT (`is it public construction under the 1994 Act` OR `is it prescribed public construction`)) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: "regarding public construction")
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@export Can the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria refer my complaint or matter to another body (Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic) s 20(1)(ib) and (k))? A complaint or matter regarding public construction may be referred, with related information, to other government agencies and bodies, including those of the Commonwealth or another State or Territory (from 17 December 2025). Any matter may be referred, as appropriate, to other bodies.
GIVEN `is it about public construction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your complaint or matter regards public construction (see the question on complaining about public construction)
      `is the other body a government agency or body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the body it would go to is a government agency or body (of Victoria, the Commonwealth, or another State or Territory)
      `does the Inspectorate consider it appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Inspectorate considers it appropriate to refer the matter to that body
      `the day of the referral` IS A DATE @desc The day the referral would be made
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Inspectorate refer my complaint to another body` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `s 20(1)(ib)` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `does the Inspectorate consider it appropriate` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: "as appropriate")
    WHERE
        `s 20(1)(ib)` MEANS
                `is it about public construction`
            AND `is the other body a government agency or body`
            AND `the day of the referral` `is on or after` `the day of the public construction amendments and s 69A`

@export May the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria, its Commissioner or its staff pass on information about me or my complaint (Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic) s 77)? A person who obtains information in their functions or powers under the Act must not disclose it unless s 77 authorises it: where reasonably necessary for their functions; in referring public construction matters or advising the Minister; to a court or VCAT in legal proceedings, or under their order; as reasonably required to investigate or enforce a law; with the written consent of the person the information relates to; where required by law; or where the Commissioner is satisfied it is in the public interest. Unauthorised disclosure is an offence (75 penalty units).
GIVEN `was it obtained under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information was obtained by the person in performing their functions or exercising their powers under the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (answer no if it was obtained under another Act the Inspectorate administers, or otherwise)
      `why is it disclosed` IS A `Why it is disclosed` @desc The circumstance of the disclosure, if any of the s 77(2) circumstances applies; your own written consent counts only for information that relates to you
      `is the Commissioner satisfied it is in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner (or the Commissioner's delegate) discloses it, being satisfied that it is in the public interest to do so (s 77(3))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May the Inspectorate pass on information about me` MEANS
    `s 77 -- the disclosure is authorised` `was it obtained under this Act` `why is it disclosed` `is the Commissioner satisfied it is in the public interest`

@export Has the government agency or body the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria referred my complaint to told the Inspectorate, in time, what it did with it (Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic) s 71)? From 17 December 2025 the Inspectorate may at any time ask an agency or body about its investigation of, or action on, a complaint or matter the Inspectorate referred to it, and the agency or body must provide the notification or information within a reasonable time, as specified by the Inspectorate. The Act gives you no right to be told yourself.
GIVEN `was my complaint referred to that agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Inspectorate referred your complaint or matter to that agency or body
      `is it a government agency or body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agency or body is a government agency or body (of Victoria, the Commonwealth, or another State or Territory)
      `did the Inspectorate ask it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Inspectorate has requested notification or information about the agency's investigation of, or action on, your complaint or matter
      `the day of the request` IS A DATE @desc The day the Inspectorate made the request
      `did the Inspectorate specify a time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Inspectorate specified the time within which the agency must answer
      `the days specified` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: the number of days from the request that the Inspectorate allowed
      `has the agency answered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agency has provided the notification or information
      `the day it answered` IS A DATE @desc If so: the day it provided it (any date otherwise)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `What became of the agency's duty`
`Has the agency answered the Inspectorate in time` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`was my complaint referred to that agency` AND `is it a government agency or body` AND `did the Inspectorate ask it`))
           THEN `the Act puts no duty on the agency on these facts`
           IF `the day of the request` `is before` `the day of the public construction amendments and s 69A`
           THEN `the Act puts no duty on the agency on these facts`
           IF (NOT `did the Inspectorate specify a time`)
           THEN `the Inspectorate specified no time: the Act says only within a reasonable time`
           OTHERWISE `what became of the agency's duty to answer` `the days specified` `has the agency answered` (`the days from` `the day of the request` `to` `the day it answered`) (`the days from` `the day of the request` `to` `today`)

@export By when must the government agency or body answer the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria's request about my referred complaint (Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic) s 71(2))? Within the time the Inspectorate specifies: the last day is that many days after the request.
GIVEN `the day of the request` IS A DATE @desc The day the Inspectorate made the request
      `the days specified` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days the Inspectorate allowed
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the agency answer the Inspectorate` MEANS `the date` `the days specified` `days after` `the day of the request`

-- s 24(1)(a), (b): the functions the Minister may not direct.
DECLARE `Which function` IS ONE OF
    `referring public construction complaints or matters, and disclosing related information, to other agencies (s 20(1)(ib))`
    `employing or engaging employees, consultants or others (s 23(1), (2), (3))`
    `another function of the Inspectorate`

@export Can the Minister direct the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria about how it handles this (Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic) s 24(1))? The Minister may give general written directions about the performance of the Inspectorate's functions, except about referring public construction complaints to other agencies, and about employing or engaging staff, consultants or others.
GIVEN `which function` IS A `Which function` @desc The function the direction would be about
      `is it a general written direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the direction is general (not about one particular complaint or person) and in writing
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Minister direct the Inspectorate about this` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`which function` EQUALS `another function of the Inspectorate`)) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `is it a general written direction` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: "general written directions")

@export Must the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria act fairly, impartially and independently in dealing with me (Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic) s 22)? In carrying out a function or power under this or any other Act it must act in a fair, impartial and independent manner; in a manner that is transparent, accountable and consistent; and in a consultative and collaborative manner as far as that is consistent with the function or power.
GIVEN `is it carrying out a function or power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Inspectorate is carrying out a function or power under the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 or any other Act in dealing with you
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must the Inspectorate act fairly and impartially with me` MEANS
    IF `is it carrying out a function or power` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

DECLARE `Who did it` IS ONE OF
    `the Commissioner`
    `an Acting Commissioner`
    `another person performing a function of the Commissioner`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `Who answers for it` IS ONE OF
    `the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria answers for it, not the person personally (s 75)`
    `s 75 does not apply on these facts: the Act does not say who answers for it`

@export If the Commissioner or someone performing the Commissioner's functions harmed me in doing their work, who answers for it (Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic) s 75)? The Commissioner, an Acting Commissioner or another person performing a function of the Commissioner is not personally liable for anything necessarily or reasonably done or omitted in good faith in performing the function, or in the reasonable belief that it was; the liability attaches instead to the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria.
GIVEN `who did it` IS A `Who did it` @desc Who did, or failed to do, the thing: the Commissioner; an Acting Commissioner; another person performing a function of the Commissioner (for example a delegate); or someone else
      `was it in performing the function` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was done or omitted in performing a function of the Commissioner under this or another Act, or in the reasonable belief that it was
      `was it necessarily or reasonably done` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was necessarily or reasonably done or omitted
      `was it in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was done or omitted in good faith
GIVETH A `Who answers for it`
`Who answers for harm the Commissioner or staff did to me` MEANS
    IF      (NOT (`who did it` EQUALS `someone else`))
        AND `was it in performing the function`
        AND `was it necessarily or reasonably done`
        AND `was it in good faith`
    THEN `the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria answers for it, not the person personally (s 75)`
    ELSE `s 75 does not apply on these facts: the Act does not say who answers for it`

§§ `Protection if I complain (s 69A)`

-- A situation: something has been done to you, or threatened, because of a complaint. The form should ask "Has someone
-- harmed you, or threatened to, because you complained or might complain to the Inspectorate?" first.

@export Is what was done or threatened to me "detriment" under the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic) s 69A(6)? Detriment includes injury, intimidation or harassment, ostracism, and damage to or loss of property. It does not include discrimination, disadvantage or adverse treatment in or in connection with employment, dismissal from or prejudice in employment, or disciplinary proceedings in employment.
GIVEN `what was done` IS A `What was done` @desc What was done or threatened: injury; intimidation or harassment; ostracism; damage to or loss of property; discrimination, disadvantage or adverse treatment in or in connection with employment; dismissal from, or prejudice in or in connection with, employment; disciplinary proceedings in or in connection with employment; or some other harm
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is it detriment under s 69A` MEANS `s 69A(6) -- detriment` `what was done`

@export Did the person "threaten to cause detriment" to me under the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic) s 69A(3)? A person threatens to cause detriment if they intend you to believe they will cause it, or are reckless as to whether you will believe it. A threat may be made by words or conduct, may be explicit or implicit, and need not be believed.
GIVEN `did they intend me to believe it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person intended that you would believe they would cause you detriment
      `were they reckless about it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person was reckless as to whether you would believe they would cause you detriment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Did they threaten to cause me detriment` MEANS `s 69A(3) -- a threat` `did they intend me to believe it` `were they reckless about it`

@export Is it an offence for someone to cause or threaten detriment to me because I complained, or might complain, to the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria (Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic) s 69A)? From 17 December 2025 a person must not cause or threaten detriment to another because they know or believe the other has made, or intends or is considering making, a complaint to the Inspectorate, has given or may give it information about public construction, or has taken or may take part in a process arising from a complaint to it. Their knowledge or belief need not be the only reason, and their belief need not be reasonable. Detriment may be direct or indirect, but treatment in employment, dismissal and discipline are not detriment under this section. Maximum penalty: 1200 penalty units or 10 years imprisonment or both.
GIVEN `the day it was done or threatened` IS A DATE @desc The day the detriment was caused or threatened
      `what was done` IS A `What was done` @desc What was done or threatened (see the question "Is it detriment under s 69A")
      `was it done or threatened` IS A `Done or threatened` @desc Whether the detriment was caused to you (directly or indirectly), or threatened, or neither
      `did they intend me to believe it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a threat: whether the person intended that you would believe they would cause you detriment
      `were they reckless about it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a threat: whether the person was reckless as to whether you would believe it
      `what they knew or believed` IS A `What they knew or believed about me` @desc What the person knew or believed about you (even if the belief was not reasonable)
      `was that one of their reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that knowledge or belief was a reason (it need not be the only reason) for causing or threatening the detriment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is it an offence to do this to me because I complained` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the day it was done or threatened` `is before` `the day of the public construction amendments and s 69A` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `s 69A(6) -- detriment` `what was done` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `was it done or threatened` EQUALS `it was threatened` AND `s 69A(3) -- a threat` `did they intend me to believe it` `were they reckless about it` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `was it done or threatened` EQUALS `neither` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
           IF `what they knew or believed` EQUALS `none of the s 69A(1) matters` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: "because")
           IF (NOT `was that one of their reasons`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: "because")
           IF `s 69A(6) -- detriment` `what was done` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (open list)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `What I must not do (s 70)`

DECLARE `What I gave` IS ONE OF
    `information`
    `a document`

@export Is it an offence for me to give this information or document to the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria (Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic) s 70)? A person must not give the Inspectorate or the Commissioner information they believe to be false or misleading in a material particular, nor produce a document they know to be false or misleading in a material particular without saying in what respect it is false or misleading and, if practicable, giving the correct information. Maximum penalty: 2 years imprisonment (1200 penalty units for a body corporate).
GIVEN `what did I give` IS A `What I gave` @desc Whether you gave information or produced a document
      `was it to the Inspectorate or the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave it to the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria or its Commissioner
      `did I believe the information false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For information: whether you believed it to be false or misleading in a material particular
      `did I know the document false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a document: whether you knew it to be false or misleading in a material particular
      `did I say in what respect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a document: whether you indicated the respect in which it is false or misleading
      `was it practicable to give the correct information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a document: whether it was practicable for you to provide the correct information
      `did I give the correct information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a document: whether you provided the correct information
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is it an offence for me to give this to the Inspectorate` MEANS
    IF (NOT `was it to the Inspectorate or the Commissioner`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
    ELSE CONSIDER `what did I give`
         WHEN `information` THEN
            IF `did I believe the information false or misleading` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: "believes")
         WHEN `a document` THEN
            BRANCH IF (NOT `did I know the document false or misleading`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: "knows")
                   IF `did I say in what respect` AND ((NOT `was it practicable to give the correct information`) OR `did I give the correct information`) THEN JUST FALSE
                   OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Penalties`

@export What is the most the fine can be, in penalty units, for an offence under the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic)? s 69A (detriment because of a complaint): 1200 penalty units; s 70 (false or misleading information or documents): 1200 penalty units for a body corporate, imprisonment only for anyone else; s 77 (unauthorised disclosure): 75 penalty units. Where the Act gives no figure, the answer is empty. The value of a penalty unit is fixed each year under the Monetary Units Act 2004.
GIVEN `which offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence
      `is the offender a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offender is a body corporate (a company) rather than an individual
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most the fine can be` MEANS `the maximum fine in penalty units for` `which offence` `is the offender a body corporate`

@export What is the longest prison term, in months, for an offence under the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic)? s 69A: 10 years (120 months); s 70: 2 years (24 months) for anyone other than a body corporate; s 77: none. A body corporate cannot be imprisoned.
GIVEN `which offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence
      `is the offender a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offender is a body corporate (a company) rather than an individual
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the longest prison term` MEANS `the maximum months of imprisonment for` `which offence` `is the offender a body corporate`

§§ `The new name (Part 6)`

@export Does a reference to the "Wage Theft Act 2020" or the "Wage Inspectorate Victoria" in my agreement or another document now mean the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 or the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria (Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic) s 80)? Unless the contrary intention appears, on and after 12 December 2025 a reference in any Act, subordinate instrument, agreement or other document is to be read that way, as far as it relates to any period after that day.
GIVEN `does a contrary intention appear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the document shows an intention that the reference keep its old meaning
      `the day the reference is applied to` IS A DATE @desc The day in the period the reference is being applied to
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the old name in my document now mean the new one` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `does a contrary intention appear` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the day the reference is applied to` `is before` `the day of the 2025 repeals and the name change` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: "any period after that commencement", fork F6)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@export Is the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria the same body as the Wage Inspectorate Victoria I complained to or dealt with (Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic) s 81)? On and after 12 December 2025 it is taken to be the same body, and no decision, matter or thing is affected by the change of name. The repeal of the wage theft offences and inspectors' powers on the same day is a different matter: s 81 saves only against the change of name.
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is it the same body as the Wage Inspectorate Victoria` MEANS
    IF `the day I am asking about` `is on or after` `the day of the 2025 repeals and the name change`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: "on and after the commencement")
